  "term": "observation",
  "definition": "Observation is attentive experience, especially a deliberately focused act of attention that often requires effort. It depends on having an object with enough stability and independence to affect the observer, and it is treated as a basic part of reasoning as well as of both observational and experimental inquiry.",
